    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32393" root="غمر" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَمِرٌ</span></b>  [part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَمِرَ</span>]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَدٌ غَمِرَةٌ</span> <i>A hand
foul with the smell of flesh-meat,</i> (S, K,) <i>and with
the grease thereof adhering to it.</i> (K.) [See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَهِكٌ</span>.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُمْرٌ</span>, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَمِرَةٌ</span> as
an epithet applied to a she-camel, see voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَبِرٌ</span>.

